## SCAN 1: Boundary / Scope Creep — Wording Fixes

The following scope-creep risks have been audited and fixed in this document:

| Risk | Current state | Fix applied |
|------|---------------|-------------|
| Stub implies real editor | Original: `quil (editor stub)` | Fixed: `quil (surface stub)` |
| Stub implies dev cockpit ownership | Doc referenced "dev cockpit" scope | Non-Goals section explicitly excludes it |
| Stub implies filesystem access | V2 Boundaries mentioned file operations | Clarified: document/file authority requires Linen OpenIntent, not included |
| Stub implies storage persistence | "Layout snapshot persistence" | Fixed: "in-memory layout snapshot (volatile, not persisted to disk)" |
| Stub implies package trust | No wording implied it, but Non-Goals didn't exclude it | Added: "No package trust assumptions" |
| Stub implies crash log viewer | No wording implied it, but Non-Goals didn't exclude it | Added: "No crash/log/dev cockpit scope" |
| Stub implies agent orchestration | PHASE_05 reference mentions Agent Mode | Non-Goals explicitly excludes agent orchestration |
| Stub owns shell focus/layout policy | Helpers follow Linen pattern exactly | Confirmed: no special-case behavior |
| Stub owns rendering policy | No rendering code exists | Non-Goals: "No rendering on surface 201 (no server)" |
| sexdisplay decides Quil lifecycle | Document: "shell-managed app surface" | Fixed: "shell-side surface identity only" — sexdisplay is not consulted for lifecycle |
| Quil writes framebuffer directly | Not mentioned anywhere | Non-Goals: "Quil cannot write framebuffer — sexdisplay is sole framebuffer writer" |
| Quil gets raw cross-PD pointers | Not mentioned anywhere | Non-Goals: "No raw cross-PD pointers" added |
| Quil bypasses Linen OpenIntent | V2 Registration suggested file nav | Clarified: document/file authority requires Linen OpenIntent in future phases |
| Quil bypasses Collar grants | Not mentioned | Non-Goals: "No capability bypass — Collar grants required for any operation" |
| Quil requires kernel/ABI/sex-pdx edits | Scope line says "No kernel/ABI/sexdisplay changes" | Confirmed — no edits needed |
| Quil introduces shared backing buffers | Not mentioned | Non-Goals: "No shared/reusable backing buffers" added |
| Quil changes surface ID allocation rules | SURFACE_ID_QUIL=201 follows existing allocation | Confirmed: 200=Linen, 201=Quil, no rule change |

